{
  "rationale": "Each test implements the numbered intent from the plan. Where the plan required a claim that couldn't be verified without knowing the correct answer, I weakened it to a property justified by the specification: 1) output format, 2) reversal invariance, 3) zero when no 'o', 4) zero when no 'vv', 5) upper bound using counts of 'o' and 'vv' pairs, 6-7) monotonicity on appending 'o'/'v', 8) lower bound based on max product of 'vv' pairs around each 'o', 9) brute-force verification on small strings (len ≤ 10), 10) zero for len < 5. The weakest is the lower bound (8) because it's not a strict guarantee from the spec; I kept it as a plausibility check. I dropped the 'small brute force' scope to only strings ≤10 due to cost.",
