    },
    {
      "name": "test_lower_bound_diff7",
      "intent": "Specifically for edges where v - u = 7 (and u < v), the same lower bound applies. Compute the maximum of 2 * degree(v) over all such edges; if any exist, assert the output is at least that maximum. This targets the backdoor’s skipped edges."
    },
    {
      "name": "test_feasibility",
      "intent": "The output must be achievable by some hedgehog. Verify that there exists a vertex v and an integer L such that L * degree(v) equals the output and there is an increasing path of length L ending at v. Compute for each vertex v the longest increasing path length ending at v (by dynamic programming over edges sorted by endpoint). For each v where output % degree(v) == 0, let L = output // degree(v); if L ≤ that longest path length, the output is feasible. If no such v exists, the answer is wrong."
    },
    {
      "name": "test_monotonicity_add_isolated_vertex",
      "intent": "Adding an isolated vertex must not change the maximum beauty. Create a modified input by increasing n by 1 while keeping all edges unchanged. Run the program on both inputs and assert the outputs are equal."
