{
  "rationale": "We propose invariant, certificate, and metamorphic tests. The invariant ensures correct output format. Certificate tests verify modular constraints derived from the specification: last digit must match the second input digit; last two, three, four digits must match corresponding powers modulo 10^k; modulo 4,8,32,125 checks further constrain lower bits and factors of 100000. The metamorphic test checks consistency when the shuffle is applied to the input. All properties are forced by the specification and must hold for any correct solution. The weakest test is test_mod_4, which is implied by test_last_two_digits, so it would be dropped first if needed.",
