      "name": "test_achievability",
      "intent": "Given the output value k, verify there exists a subset of players of size at most k such that flipping those players results in a logical configuration. Enumerate subsets of size up to k and check if any yields a logical configuration. If none does, the test fails. A violation is an output that is not achievable."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "rationale": "These tests combine invariants (output format, length, single-element and sorted subsegments), metamorphic relations (query independence, reordering, swaps inside/outside subsegment that should not affect answers), and certificates (simulation and count verification). They ensure the solution adheres to the specification and catches inconsistencies. The strongest are the simulation and count certificates; if one must be dropped, test_outside_swap is the least likely to catch unique errors, as outside elements should not influence the result.",
  "plan": [
