{
  "rationale": "The output for each query must be the cycle lengths of the permutation. The tests are designed to catch deviations using necessary conditions: bounds (1), output shape (2,10), consistency within cycles (3,4), exact cycle length via minimality and permutation closure (5), invariance under conjugation (6,9) and inversion (7), and divisibility of frequencies (8). Each property is forced by the specification: e.g., a_i must equal a_{p_i} because they share a cycle; conjugation preserves cycle structure; inverse has same cycle lengths; the minimal day of return must satisfy the divisor condition. The strongest catch is test_minimality; the weakest is test_bounds. If one test must be dropped, test_conjugation_shift is redundant with test_conjugation_reverse.",
