{
  "rationale": "I built each test based on the plan's intent, using only what the specification guarantees, without solving the problem. For each intent: 1) output format is exactly 'YES\n' or 'NO\n' (invariant). 2) When C=0, answer must be YES (spec: choose one multiple of A, sum is multiple of A, modulo B is 0). 3) When A multiple of B, answer YES iff C=0 (spec: multiples of A are multiples of B, so sums mod B are 0). 4) A=1: YES always (spec: choose 1). 5) B=1: YES always (spec: C=0, any sum works). 6) Metamorphic: (A+B,B,C) same as (A,B,C) (spec: adding B to A doesn't change residues mod B). 7) Metamorphic: (2A,2B,2C) same as (A,B,C) (spec: scaling by 2 preserves divisibility/residue relationships). 8) Certificate: if YES, there exists S in [1,B] with A*S ≡ C mod B (spec: we can take at most B multiples to cover residues). 9) Metamorphic: if YES for (A,B,C), then YES for (A,B,(C+A) mod B) (spec: adding one more multiple of A). 10) Metamorphic: if YES for (A,B,C), then YES for (A,B,(2C) mod B) (spec: doubling the sum of selected multiples). All assertions rely strictly on specification properties, not on unseen code.",
  "tests": [
    {
      "name": "test_output_format",
      "source": "def test_output_format(run, x):
