    {
      "name": "test_certificate",
      "intent": "The expected second-highest equals the sum over x of the probability that at least two bids are at least x. Compute this sum directly from the input: for each x from 1 to 10000, compute P(X_i >= x) for each bidder, then compute P(at least two) = 1 - P(none) - P(exactly one). Sum these probabilities. Assert that the program's output equals this sum within 1e-9 relative or absolute error."
    },
    {
      "name": "test_monotonic_add",
      "intent": "Adding a bidder cannot decrease the expected second-highest. If the input has n < 5, create a new input by appending a copy of the first bidder's range (so n increases by 1). Run the program on both and assert that the output for the augmented input is at least the original output minus 1e-9."
    },
    {
      "name": "test_possible_bounds",
      "intent": "The expected second-highest must lie between the smallest and largest possible values of the second-highest bid. Compute the minimum possible second-highest as the smallest integer v such that at least two bidders' ranges contain v. Compute the maximum possible second-highest as the largest integer v such that at least two ranges contain v. Assert that the program's output is in the closed interval [min_possible - 1e-9, max_possible + 1e-9]."
    },
