{
  "rationale": "The tests combine basic sanity checks (length, character set, lexicographic order), a certificate for the easy k>n case, metamorphic relations that modify the input without affecting the answer (appending/duplicating s), and necessary conditions for minimality (next-string property, prefix monotonicity, and the no-smaller-candidate check). These cover common error patterns like off-by-one in increment, mishandling of carries, using wrong alphabet, and non-minimal answers. The metamorphic tests catch dependence on parts of s that should not matter. The no-smaller-candidate test is a strong necessary condition that would fail if the output is not the smallest possible. We would drop test_upper_bound first as it is the weakest.",
