{
  "rationale": "These tests target subtle bugs, including a suspected backdoor that blocks moves into row 2. Symmetry catches asymmetry when start is row 2 and end is not. Translation invariance detects dependence on absolute coordinates. Adjacency catches blocked direct moves. Upper/lower bounds guard against extreme values. Redundancy and merge/split tests ensure robustness to segment representation. Monotonicity ensures adding cells does not increase distance. If forced to drop one, the split segment test is least likely to catch the backdoor but helps overall correctness.",
