  "rationale": "These tests combine boundedness, invariants, metamorphic relations, and a certificate to catch errors. Non‑negativity and upper bound catch off‑by‑one and overflow. Parity catches miscounts mod 2. Bit‑flip and reversal invariance catch symmetry bugs. Swap invariance catches errors when |a|=|b|. Lower bound max contribution catches underestimation. Removal relations catch off‑by‑one in window enumeration. The integer check is basic sanity. All properties follow directly from the specification. If a test must be dropped, drop the integer check as it is the weakest.",
  "plan": [
    {
      "name": "test_non_negative",
      "intent": "Assert that the output is a non‑negative integer, because each Hamming distance is a sum of non‑negative values."
    },
    {
      "name": "test_upper_bound",
      "intent": "Assert that the output does not exceed len(a) * (len(b) ‑ len(a) + 1), the maximum possible sum given the number of substrings and their maximum Hamming distance."
    },
    {
      "name": "test_parity",
      "intent": "Assert that the parity of the output matches the computed parity derived from popcount(a) and the weighted sum of bits in b, a necessary condition for any correct sum of Hamming distances."
    },
    {
      "name": "test_bit_flip_invariant",
      "intent": "Assert that flipping all bits in both a and b leaves the output unchanged, because the Hamming distance between complementary strings is identical."
    },
    {
      "name": "test_reversal_invariant",
      "intent": "Assert that reversing both a and b leaves the output unchanged, as the multiset of aligned character pairs remains the same."
    },
    {
      "name": "test_swap_invariant",
      "intent": "When |a| = |b|, assert that swapping a and b yields the same output, since there is only one substring and Hamming distance is symmetric."
    },
    {
      "name": "test_lower_bound_max_contribution",
      "intent": "Assert that the output is at least the maximum over i of the contribution of position i, computed directly from b as the number of mismatches at that position across all windows."
    },
