{
  "rationale": "Each test implements the intent strictly using property-based checks derivable solely from the specification, without computing the correct output. Strengthened when possible: test_line_length_and_chars now also ensures each line length equals n (spec demands n×n matrix). Weakened when necessary: test_metamorphic_inner_core only applies for n≥5 (spec defines odd n>1, so n=3 would be invalid for that relation). All tests rely on properties explicitly stated or implied: matrix size, symmetry, diamond contiguity, and recursive structure for n≥5. Dropping test_vertical_symmetry would be least harmful because it's subsumed by transpose_symmetry and palindrome checks.",
  "tests": [
    {
      "name": "test_line_count",
      "source": "def test_line_count(run, x):
