{
  "rationale": "I implemented each intent as a property test using only the specification, without computing the correct answer. Strengthened or weakened as needed: (1)-(2) are direct invariants; (3) upper bound derived from digit count; (4) metamorphic relation using f(n); (5) certificate by simulating steps; (6) small-n exhaustive check; (7) relation between n and f(n) outputs; (8)-(9) special-case invariants for powers of 10 and all-nines; (10) scaling relation using 10*n. Each test holds for any correct solution on any valid input. If I had to drop one, I'd drop test_small_n_bruteforce because it only covers n ≤ 100000, but the given inputs include larger numbers, making it vacuous for many cases—still safe as it just skips larger inputs.",
  "tests": [
    {
      "name": "test_single_digit_invariant",
      "source": "def test_single_digit_invariant(run, x):
