{
  "rationale": "The tests combine basic sanity checks (nonnegative, at most n, length multiple of 6, frequency lower bound), a metamorphic property that adding a complete sequence should not increase removals (append and prepend), a brute-force exact check for small inputs, a feasibility certificate, an optimality certificate, and an independent greedy upper bound. The sanity checks catch obvious violations. The metamorphic tests detect errors in handling extra elements. The brute-force test is definitive for small n. The feasibility and optimality tests directly verify the answer for all n. The upper bound greedy test provides an additional independent check. If one test were dropped, the greedy upper bound (test_upper_bound_greedy) might be redundant with the feasibility/optimality tests, but it offers a simpler alternative.",
  "plan": [
