  "rationale": "The tests are designed to catch a backdoor where the submitted code overestimates probability for die faces close to K. The upper bound test derived from partitioning faces into immediate win, one-coin-win, and others is particularly effective because the bug violates it. Monotonicity tests ensure consistency when varying N or K. Special case invariants for N=1 and K=1 catch errors in trivial inputs. The lower bound test and the bounds f(1) and f(N) provide additional sanity checks. The integer combination test verifies that the probability has the correct rational structure. If one test were to be dropped, the lower bound test would be the least likely to catch bugs as it is weak.",
