{
  "rationale": "Each test corresponds to one intent from the plan, justified by the specification's constraints: feasibility, optimality, lower/upper bounds, symmetry, monotonicity, range, integer parsing, and consistency. Strengthened where necessary: test_feasibility uses output T to verify all prizes reachable; test_optimality ensures T minimal by checking a prize forces T; test_monotonic_add inserts a new prize at smallest available ≥2 (ensuring valid input); test_symmetry constructs symmetric input by mapping x → 1e6+1-x (preserving distinctness and ordering). Weakened where specification alone insufficient: test_consistency_bounds combines earlier checks. All tests are property-based, rely only on input/output and spec, never recompute answer. If dropping one, test_consistency_bounds is redundant with 3&4, but kept as per plan.",
  "tests": [
    {
      "name": "test_feasibility",
      "source": "def test_feasibility(run, x):
