{
  "rationale": "The tests combine direct verification with metamorphic relations and specific invariants to catch backdoors. Full verification computes great choices directly from the specification. Metamorphic tests check consistency under permutations of A, B, D (which fix the default C) and under length-preserving character substitutions, as the algorithm depends only on lengths. Invariants cover the edge case of all equal lengths and the necessary condition that non-C outputs must have extremal lengths. These properties are all forced by the specification. If a test were dropped, test_case_insensitivity could be omitted as it is similar to test_replace_with_as.",
  "plan": [
