{
  "rationale": "The specification implies the answer is always 0 or 1: 0 if the start and end airports share a company, 1 otherwise. This follows because when companies differ, there must be an adjacent pair of different companies, allowing a cost-1 path via free same-company flights. The tests verify this through invariants (output format, bounds), certificates (conditions on a, b, and companies), and metamorphic relations (symmetries under flipping companies, reversal, and swapping start/end). The direct formula test provides a complete check. Together they catch any deviation from the correct logic.",
  "plan": [
