{
  "rationale": "We design tests to catch missing values, extra values, formatting errors, and off-by-one mistakes. Each test is derived from the specification: the conditions on x, the completeness of the set, and a metamorphic relation that holds for valid inputs. The tests should catch the backdoor that truncates the output when the number of solutions is 10^5+1. If we had to drop one, it would be test_count_bound as it is the weakest and covered by others.",
  "plan": [
    {
      "name": "test_format",
