{
  "rationale": "We design tests to catch undercounts and overcounts, especially the suspected backdoor that reduces count for words starting with 'Z' and having exactly two capitals. The per-word lower bound test will catch any undercount, and the existence test catches overcounts. Metamorphic tests ensure consistency under transformations that should not affect the maximum. Boundedness tests ensure basic sanity. If we had to drop one, we would drop the total capitals bound as it is the weakest and redundant with other bounds.",
